BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 438.32 Tm (Items: Leave cosmetic items like paint and carpet at the door. Use the inspection contingency for water heater straps,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.10 Tm (HVAC, plumbing and electrical issues, so a seller refusal on real defects becomes a clean exit with the deposit [Andrew) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.87 Tm (Finney Team - ND7J57hzroE @ 00:02:01]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 392.65 Tm (On a 10-day inspection period where the seller will not give credits or a price cut, make sure the contract is cancelled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 377.42 Tm (by day 9 or day 10 [Larry Mastropieri - CSHBzTZo3Yc @ 00:00:45]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 362.20 Tm (Only wire on instructions that came directly from the title company. When texts or emails arrive, call title yourself) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.97 Tm (rather than waiting for a call [The Treasure Valley Home Show - 5lKK7iczAKk @ 00:38:18]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 331.75 Tm (On low-down-payment programs the deposit can come back at closing: CCM zero-down buyers got all of it back, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 316.52 Tm (an Idaho Housing buyer got all but $500 [The Treasure Valley Home Show - 5lKK7iczAKk @ 00:04:17]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 294.30 Tm (Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.07 Tm (The deposit number itself is where operators split hardest. Kristie Dimarakis runs a flat 3% script, pegging a $650,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 256.85 Tm (offer at a $19,500 good faith deposit as the default way to show the seller you are serious about buying their home) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.62 Tm ([NwZ7Oa8GUXQ @ 00:00:38]. The Treasure Valley team in Idaho works off roughly 1% on resale and spec homes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.40 Tm (about $5,000 on a half-million-dollar house, and will deliberately write just $500 on a 100% VA deal when the buyer's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.17 Tm (account does not show the cash, rather than letting a borrowed $5,000 suddenly appear and trigger a sourcing fight later) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 195.95 Tm ([5lKK7iczAKk @ 00:22:02]. Charles Nedder sits at the opposite pole: Greenwich custom is 10% at contract signing,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 180.72 Tm (which means a $200,000 wire on a $2 million home, often within five days of an accepted offer, and the deal is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 165.50 Tm (secure until that wire lands [xyiyeiBkCqQ @ 00:01:49]. Robert Greenblatt argues the dollar figure is legally trivial,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 150.27 Tm (since a New Jersey contract can technically be held with $1 of consideration, but psychologically decisive: a buyer with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 135.05 Tm ($1,000 at risk may walk the moment nerves hit, while a buyer with $20,000 sitting in escrow is far less likely to bail, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 119.82 Tm (the amount itself sends the seller a commitment message [CCWuS-x3COc @ 00:00:58].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 104.60 Tm (Operators also split on who sits on the money and what it takes to pry it loose. Katie Anderson routes Pensacola) Tj ET
