BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 528.10 Tm (Davis lived that exact mismatch early on, using a statement from a father's line of credit on bank-owned offers; it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 512.87 Tm (worked 99% of the time, and the one or two challenges were settled by explaining the lender was a money partner) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 497.65 Tm ([FOfp5iWKVkc @ 00:02:51]. The heavier trap is REO inventory, where Davis says acceptance depends on the bank,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 482.42 Tm (and some will refuse a transactional funding letter on a cash offer and demand an actual bank statement or a line of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 467.20 Tm (credit that is ready to go [FUjDeT5p55I @ 00:01:08]. The back end fails too: Foreclosure University warns that the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 451.97 Tm (investor must stay independent because the end buyer's money cannot fund the A-to-B leg, and that a closing agent or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 436.75 Tm (attorney who does not know the backtack process has to be replaced or shown exactly what to do [38RXOgdabuQ @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 421.52 Tm (00:02:23]. Every one of these surfaces after the seller signs, which is the most expensive moment to discover them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 406.30 Tm (Wire fraud losses are the hardest numbers on the table. Sunny Fedorenko cites a Southern California couple who lost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 391.07 Tm ($160,000 and an Orlando couple who lost $38,000 in escrow scams, and says that once a wire is gone the bank, the title) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.85 Tm (company and the agent are not responsible [j0SpK9C7lHs @ 00:02:21]. Think Escrow describes a buyer in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 360.62 Tm (multiple-offer bidding war who got a fake escrow email demanding an immediate good-faith deposit to lock in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 345.40 Tm (purchase, rushed to the bank, drove home happy, and in a matter of half an hour the funds were already diverted into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 330.17 Tm (out-of-state accounts [f-7Rw_JAZOA @ 00:10:18]. The same escrow veteran recounts an escrow company that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 314.95 Tm (skipped looking at its outgoing wires for several days while fraudsters inside its accounting system generated wires in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 299.72 Tm ($10,000 and $20,000 increments totaling about $250,000 [f-7Rw_JAZOA @ 00:07:41]. PropLogix's title expert was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 284.50 Tm (spoofed supposedly ordering an office to wire a large sum, a request built from one internet search of name, email) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 269.27 Tm (address and company [k03c-6thJPg @ 00:01:46]. Fedorenko adds that hackers now use AI mimicry: cloned signatures,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 254.05 Tm (hijacked threads, fake PDFs carrying escrow logos, and URLs identical except for one letter. Every loss above started) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 238.82 Tm (with a message that looked legitimate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 223.60 Tm (The closing math hides its own traps, and they hit cash to close directly. Matthew Halliday of Escrow Escapes tells of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 208.37 Tm (buyer holding the pen who found an extra $800 that turned out to be a special assessment, not routine HOA dues, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 193.15 Tm (rejects the 'just sign and sort it out later' instinct because an unclear amount does not get clearer once the keys are in) Tj ET
